* Suspected acute viral respiratory infection, defined per European Conference on Infections in Leukemia (ECIL) criteria as meeting all of the following: clinical suspicion recorded in the electronic health record; positive multiplex PCR for RSV, SARS-CoV-2, or influenza; and fulfillment of criteria for either upper (URTI) or lower respiratory tract infection (LRTI).

* URTI criteria: presence of at least two of the following - rhinorrhea, nasal or sinus congestion, otitis media, pharyngitis, or dry cough - with a normal chest X-ray or CT scan.
* LRTI or new pneumonia criteria: cough accompanied by at least one of the following - dyspnea, rhonchi, crackles, wheezing, tachypnea, or hypoxemia - with a new pulmonary infiltrate on chest X-ray or CT scan.

